SUMMARY:Deadline: Movies that Matter Festival 2027: Film Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Movies that Matter\, the human rights film festival in The Hagu
 e (19-27 March 2027)\, is open for 2027 submissions. The festival screens 
 poignant fiction films and revealing documentaries that stir debates about
  human rights\, sustainability and the fight against injustice\, and feeds
  several competitions: the Grand Jury Documentary Competition (eight docum
 entaries\, EUR 5\,000\, winner eligible for Academy Award consideration fo
 r Best Documentary Feature)\, Grand Jury Fiction (EUR 5\,000)\, Shorts (EU
 R 1\,500)\, plus Activist Lens\, Justice Frame\, Dutch Focus\, an Educatio
 n Award and an Audience Award. ELIGIBILITY: films of any length\, complete
 d or world-premiering in 2026 or 2027\, addressing human rights and/or soc
 ial or environmental issues\; English commentary/dialogue or English subti
 tles required\; the film must not have been released in Dutch cinemas\, br
 oadcast on Dutch television\, made freely available online\, or submitted 
 to the festival before. A world premiere is not required but may be taken 
 into account in selection. FEES: EUR 25 normal fee until 30 September 2026
 \, EUR 35 late fee from 1 October\; final deadline 1 November 2026. Select
 ion is announced at the end of February 2027. Submit via the festival's ow
 n submission database at database.moviesthatmatter.nl. Note the festival a
 lso runs a separate Take on Film & Impact industry programme (deadline 11 
 October 2026) for feature documentaries in late/post-production\, but it c
 arries no cash and participants fund their own travel\, so it is not liste
 d on the desk.\n\nOrganisation: Movies that Matter\nLocation: The Hague\, 
 Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; submissions open worldwide\, att
 endance not required for submission.\nAward: Cash prizes: EUR 5\,000 Grand
  Jury Documentary award (winner also becomes eligible for consideration fo
 r the Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature)\, EUR 5\,000 Grand Jury 
 Fiction award\, and EUR 1\,500 Shorts award\; further competitions (Activi
 st Lens\, Justice Frame\, Dutch Focus\, Education Award\, Audience Award) 
 publish no amounts. SUBMISSION FEE: EUR 25 until 30 September 2026\, EUR 3
 5 late fee 1 October to 1 November 2026\; fee waivers only in very excepti
 onal cases.\n\nMore: https://moviesthatmatter.nl/en/festival/industry/film
 -submissions/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://moviesthatmatter.nl/en/festival/industry/film-submissions/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; submissions 
 open worldwide\, attendance not required for submission.
END:VEVENT
